A||N||4||FIL||Is my throttle body original?||||5||
Z||000000||FIL||12-16-2001||12:53 PM||||I purchased an 87 GT of a guy who purchased it off his brother.  His brother did some performance work on it because he was all into the rally racing.  I can't get a hold of both of them to ask certain questions about my car.  Now my car has 160k miles on it.  It runs SO strong, I can't believe it.  It has after market wires and ignition, ported exhaust, after market koni springs.  Here is were my question comes in....I was looking at the throttle body of it and noticed the word "Holley" on the top of it.  My question is, did the original throttle bodies had that word on them or is mine also an aftermarket part?  Also how would I know it this guy installed a power pulley by just looking at it?  I want to buy some more perfomance parts but I don't want to buy parts that he has already bought.  One more thing...Is it worth the money to buy an intake for it?  Do any one know of any homemade plans on making one?....    ||||reg||5
Z||000001||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-16-2001||01:05 PM||||Believe it or not the Holley is STOCK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||12-16-2001||01:34 PM||||Welcome to PFF. As I understand it the factory intake is quite efficient. It already sucks outside air.  However if you want something different some of the parts vendors (links at the top of the page) sell them.  Or you can build your own <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-009138.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-009138.html</A> <BR>Have fun with your Fiero, sounds like some cool stuff has already been done to it.<BR>Gary||||reg||7
Z||000003||Fierokid87||12-16-2001||07:35 PM||||Yes All Fiero V-6's came with the Holley TB.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid-xmas-sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIL||12-18-2001||09:59 AM||||Thanks guys for the heads up.  I thought that, being a Holley, that it was aftermarket stuff.  Oh well, know I know what to start looking for.<BR>||||reg||14
